        ["search_modifications_declared"] = new TableDoc("SearchModification", "One modification the search task DECLARED -- what the engine was configured to look for, not what it could have found and not what it placed (G28). The distinction is not pedantic: all three ingested datasets declare 33 UNIMOD accessions while their peptidoforms carry 16, 46 and 57, and `UNIMOD:45` and `UNIMOD:422` are PLACED in all three while appearing in no declaration at all -- found twice, independently, from the GPTMD-over-UniProt direction (dataRepo 021 section 6) and from the terminal-motif direction (aging 024 section 4). The table is honestly \"what the search task declared\", which is a useful thing to hold, PROVIDED nothing believes it is \"what the search could have found\". Both halves are named explicitly so the difference survives the naming (aging 024 section 6): this is the `_declared` table, and `search_modifications_placed` is the derived counterpart. A J8-style mass-silent check reads the PLACED one.",
